      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That tension is palpable because early training runs often involved proprietary, non-public heuristics that stabilized the momentum while public papers focused only on the asymptotic behavior. The \"sterilized\" version you are analyzing lacks those specific, often hyper-parameter sensitive, safeguards that prevented the model from diverging entirely before it ever reached the claimed scaling efficiency. It appears the community prioritized reproducible scaling curves over admitting the brittle, hand-tuned initialization pipelines that made large-scale training possible in the first place.",
